SnmpLab — dual release

This repository is published as a MIXED release:

OPEN / reference (release/open/)
    The neutral protocol contracts (SnmpContracts), documentation and a reference
    example are published as source. They describe the wire format and how the
    stack is composed. License: MIT (see below).

    The standalone license-gate stub (open-reference/stub/) is published the same
    way: it is an independent work that reproduces the startup check against the
    author's PUBLIC key and refuses to run without an author-signed token. It is
    not the license guard, and its source is not the guard's source.

CLOSED / product (release/product/)
    The management engine (SnmpNms), the SNMP driver (SnmpDriver), the simulator
    (SnmpSimulator), the license guard (SnmpLicensing) and the operator apps are
    distributed ONLY as compiled, obfuscated binaries. Their source is NOT
    published. Running them requires a valid, author-signed license token; without
    one the product refuses to start.

License
    - The OPEN reference (SnmpContracts, docs, example, license-gate stub): MIT License.
    - The CLOSED product (compiled binaries + the license guard): proprietary.
      It is source-available to the author only. Use, redistribution, modification
      or operation without a valid signed license granted by the author is
      prohibited and terminates any right to use it.

Enforcement
    The product embeds a license guard (Ed25519/ECDSA P-256 signed token). It never
    contacts the network and sends nothing; it only verifies the signed license at
    startup and blocks if it is missing, malformed, tampered with, or expired.

    Author tool: LicenseTool (gen-keys | sign | verify) issues licenses.
